# p05 the height measurement was attempted and produced no datum
#
# LinkML option: none. The repo's crosswalk (docs/crosswalk.md, cause c) puts this outside the
# six options because it is a fact about a process, not about a field.
#
# Live discussion: https://github.com/obi-ontology/obi/issues/1230
#   "Provide patterns for relating absence of actionable data with assay 'successfulness'"
#   (open since 2020-09-06). See the template rdf-examples/p05_failed_assay.ttl for the positions
#   recorded there.
#
# No subclasses of COB:0000083 'failed planned process'. James A. Overton gave that position on the
# OBI developer call of 2026-09-14 (relayed by Mark Miller). So the attempt is an instance of
# COB:0000083 itself, and the intended assay type is given with COB:0000085, not with a
# 'failed height measurement' class.
#
# What exists (checked 2026-09-14): COB:0000083 'failed planned process' (subclass of COB:0000082,
# disjoint with COB:0000035 in COB 2025-12-15 and OBI 2026-07-27) and COB:0000085 'intended plan
# process type', an object property with a label and no definition, domain, or range. It is used
# here as the closest existing term, pointing at the OBI:0003817 assay class by punning.
#
# Consequences of the current axioms, shown by ROBOT (README):
#   - The attempt cannot be typed OBI:0003817 'length measurement assay': every assay is a
#     COB:0000035, which is disjoint with COB:0000083.
#   - It cannot use OBI:0000293 'has specified input' for Napoleon: its domain is COB:0000035. So
#     he is linked with RO:0000057 'has participant'. See p05_failed_assay_contradiction.ttl.
#
# A consumer can infer that a height measurement of Napoleon was attempted during examination 1
# and did not complete, so there is no datum to look for. They cannot infer why it failed.

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/napoleon/> .
@prefix BFO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix RO:   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_> .
@prefix OBI:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_> .
@prefix COB:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_> .

ex:heightAssay1 a owl:NamedIndividual , COB:0000083 ;
    rdfs:label "failed height measurement attempt 1 (invented)" ;
    COB:0000085 OBI:0003817 ;              # intended plan process type (punned class)
    BFO:0000050 ex:examination1 ;
    RO:0000057 ex:napoleon , ex:physician1 .
    # no OBI:0000299 has specified output
